itle":"Verify the dedicated voice project","instructions":"Confirm the exact provider organization, dedicated workspace project, supported voice model, transport and selected voice. Verify current credentials, provider capability, privacy disclosures, retention and website fallback using actual provider evidence.\n\nSave credentials in Receptionist connections. Prepare the exact website voice proposal with reviewed provider and inquiry evidence, funding scope and cost bounds or the explicitly approved owner budget policy. Do not infer provider acceptance from a saved key."},{"title":"Complete the business content review","instructions":"Use the Business setup view for the greeting, full policy, optional concise voice policy, services, answers, inquiries, hours and limits. Keep any appointment mapping separately reviewed.\n\nSave an inactive draft, inspect its content comparison, and apply only the reviewed version against an accepted compatible baseline. A later configuration, connection or credential change needs its actual current review; do not reuse stale identities."},{"title":"Review accounting and available capacity","instructions":"Open Founder advanced operations and accounting. Read current accounting and recovery for the exact settings owner and configuration.\n\nRecord a reconciled period opening and accounting admission only from actual dated evidence, using the existing reviewed operations. Keep cash, service consumption and voice usage distinct. Blank or unresolved provider amounts remain unknown. Delayed-overrun risk needs the explicit current accepted policy; a guide edit or budget number cannot provide that acceptance."},{"title":"Recover an expired test call when required","instructions":"Use the original call ID and its original pinned configuration to read local retirement metadata. Confirm that the actual provider call has ended when that evidence is available.\n\nPrepare the exact retirement review with its dated evidence and reason, independently review it, preview the planned change, apply it, and read back the result. Local retirement releases eligible application capacity; it does not establish provider closure or erase usage, charges or reservations. Resolve any remaining accounting hold through the existing reviewed recovery controls. Never clear a record merely because no new charge appeared."},{"title":"Accept the restricted configuration","instructions":"Review and accept the exact provider, credential, inquiry and accounting evidence through the existing Operation reviews flow. Acceptance and application are separate steps.\n\nRead the applied configuration and current readiness. Keep public acceptance separate from restricted testing, and preserve the owner's pause until the required checks allow a controlled test. Provider, accounting or capability uncertainty must stay visible."},{"title":"Open one fresh restricted test window","instructions":"Prepare the application test window with explicit UTC start and end times, actual restricted-route evidence, its fingerprint and observation time. The window is at most one hour and cannot be extended or replaced for that accepted configuration.\n\nReview and apply the exact window. Enable owner permission only when ready, and confirm the intended caller route is restricted. Schedule the human test inside the actual window and reception hours."},{"title":"Verify two-way voice and slot reuse","instructions":"Start the restricted voice test. Verify human-heard audio in both directions, the AI introduction, interruption and correction handling, accurate approved answers, truthful inquiry results and the appropriate fallback.\n\nEnd the call, verify the application slot is released, and start a second call after the configured start interval. Inspect unresolved provider and accounting states separately. Preserve the actual result; test-window presence or a provider status alone is not call-quality acceptance."},{"title":"Complete separate public activation